# Folder Structure (SHM)

Only create folders and files that fit this project’s structure.

## Allowed top-level under `src/`

```text
App/           # Root app and router (App/index.tsx)
api/           # API client and endpoint constants (client.ts, endpoints.ts, index.ts)
components/    # UI components (ui/, layout/, features/)
contexts/      # React contexts (e.g. auth-context.tsx)
constants/     # App-wide constants (e.g. routes, config values)
hooks/         # Custom hooks (useApi.ts, feature hooks, feature/use*-page.ts)
pages/         # Thin page components only
schemas/       # Zod (and similar) validation schemas
styles/        # Global CSS
types/         # Shared TypeScript types and interfaces
utils/         # Pure helpers and auth utilities (e.g. auth-utils.ts)
```

## Under `components/`

- **`ui/`** – Shadcn primitives only; kebab-case files (e.g. `button.tsx`, `card.tsx`).
- **`layout/`** – Layout pieces (sidebar, header, etc.).
- **`features/`** – One folder per feature (e.g. `timeline/`, `golden-temple/`, `ten-gurus/`). Each has feature-specific components and an `index.ts` barrel that re-exports public components.

## Under `hooks/`

- **Root** – Shared hooks: `useApi.ts`, `useToast.ts`, feature data hooks (e.g. `useSikhApps.ts`, `useTimeline.ts`).
- **Feature folders** – One folder per screen/feature when the hook is large or screen-specific: `hooks/timeline/useTimelinePage.ts`, `hooks/golden-temple/useGoldenTemplePage.ts`, `hooks/ten-gurus/useTenGurusPage.ts`.

## Do not create

- `src/common/`, `src/helpers/`, `src/lib/`, `src/services/` → use `utils/` or `api/` as appropriate.
- `src/ui/` at top level → use `src/components/ui/`.
- `src/config/` for API client → use `src/api/`.
- `config/queryClient.ts` or TanStack Query setup → this project uses `useAPI` only.

## Path alias

- Use **`@/`** for `src/` (e.g. `@/api`, `@/components/features/timeline`, `@/hooks/useApi`, `@/types`). No deep relative paths like `../../../components`.
